+// Chrome's fullscreen and pointer lock state talks to this. A page's fullscreen reaches the shell through the page
+// (-webContents:didChangeFullscreen:), and the shell takes the window in and out of macOS fullscreen as it does on CEF. So entering and
+// leaving here only record what Chrome asked for: Chrome's controller reads IsFullscreen right after asking, before the window's
